title: 'Abstracts away HRMP deposits into a Deposit Provider impl. Paves way for remote deposits later (on CT)'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The relay chain HRMP pallet no longer reserves channel deposits directly. Every call that takes
    or gives back one sends a `DepositChangeRequest` to `hrmp::Config::DepositProvider`, a
    `hrmp::deposits::ChannelDepositProvider`. A provider that applies the request within the call
    answers `Applied` and the call completes right away; one that holds the funds on another chain
    answers `Pending` and the call completes later through `OnDepositSet`. The pallet
    implements `ChannelDepositProvider` itself for deposits held in `Config::Currency`, so
    `type DepositProvider = Hrmp;` keeps the behaviour of today. Every runtime must now set it.

    `OpenChannelRequested`, `OpenChannelAccepted` and `OpenChannelDepositsUpdated` are now emitted
    once the call completes. As a result `force_open_hrmp_channel`, `establish_system_channel` and
    `establish_channel_with_system` now also emit `OpenChannelRequested` and `OpenChannelAccepted`.

    Prepares for taking deposits in `pallet-hrmp-para` on the Coretime chain.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
